      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "To structure these metrics, quantify \"neighborhood volatility\" using metrics like census data changes (e.g., housing turnover, crime rate fluctuations) over several years. For \"community cohesion,\" you could use proxies such as volunteer rates, neighborhood association activity levels, or local networking data if available. Normalizing these features—perhaps using Z-scores or Min-Max scaling—is crucial before integrating them into your prediction model. This standardization allows the model to weigh them fairly against traditional credit data.",
